cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ResolveLab or its published evidence, please cite it as below."
title: "ResolveLab: fault-injected tool environments with side-effect grading for agent evaluation and post-training"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Huang
    given-names: Allen
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ta0p1/ResolveLab"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - agent evaluation
  - tool use
  - fault injection
  - imitation learning
  - DAgger
  - LLM post-training
abstract: >-
  ResolveLab runs tool-using LLM agents against real HTTP services that inject failures
  (conflicts, rate limits, lost acknowledgements, revoked permissions, prompt injection) and
  grades episodes from server state and the commit log. Its v0.4 study registers and
  tests DAgger against a size-matched behaviour-cloning control with replayable evidence.
